      "id": 61025945,
      "body": "Product thinking is a valuable skill that complements all roles. From my experience working in product, I’ve seen how crucial it is for making informed decisions. Dogfooding is great—if you're an engineer, watch sales calls, spend time with the product team, and observe new feature demos. You'll gain insights to guide future direction, identify inefficiencies, and plan for better scaling.\n\nAlso, apply this mindset to all products you use daily. Analyze how each one solves problems and consider the designers' decisions. This helps develop a strong product sense and reveals nuances in even seemingly simple elements.",
